  "title": "LOG_OPENAI_MATH_STAGE38_REVIEW",
  "revisionId": "AHj4eMSacRkBI3XBzfAn4R9V6t5dtvyTROZBO8DDTEkMTBVVPPTvtBu8NoevIZdjKkhvcyVTIanQlZRjw_-1xOY7pxxhPJHy123N423hYeo",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "Stage38 — openai/math 全体レビュー",
      "startIndex": 1,
      "endIndex": 29,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "TITLE",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "STATUS = NONCREDIT_EXTERNAL_METHOD_RESEARCH",
      "startIndex": 30,
      "endIndex": 73,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "TARGET = K16-C3-CAMPEDELLI-UNIFORM-TORSOR / R29-CAMP2",
      "startIndex": 74,
      "endIndex": 127,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "DRIVE_AUTHORITY_RETAINED = CAMPEDELLI_RESULTS + CAMPEDELLI_WORKING + later CT/PARI review logs",
      "startIndex": 128,
      "endIndex": 222,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "NO receiver / theorem / endpoint / perfect-cuboid credit.",
      "startIndex": 223,
      "endIndex": 280,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "openai/math source lock = commit adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a",
      "startIndex": 281,
      "endIndex": 354,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Stage38 current frontier",
      "startIndex": 356,
      "endIndex": 380,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Retained Stage38 state:",
      "startIndex": 381,
      "endIndex": 404,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- R-11: arbitrary-support Sel2 is the nullity of a tripartite Legendre adjacency matrix.",
      "startIndex": 405,
      "endIndex": 493,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- R-12/R-13: parity, part-imbalance lower bound, and the diagonal type-span obstruction.",
      "startIndex": 494,
      "endIndex": 582,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- R-14: on the special factor shape, B=-1 gives dim Sel2=2 and B=+1 gives dim Sel2=4.",
      "startIndex": 583,
      "endIndex": 668,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- Later CT work: in a tested B=+1 population, a nondegenerate Cassels-Tate pairing on Sel2/E[2] certifies MW rank 0 for 53 fibers; CT-zero fibers remain ambiguous without deeper 4-Selmer/second descent information.",
      "startIndex": 669,
      "endIndex": 883,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- Global bottlenecks remain: infinitude/uniformity in u, control of CT-zero/dim4 fibers, and conversion of fixed-fiber elliptic exclusions into a uniform Campedelli quotient obstruction.",
      "startIndex": 884,
      "endIndex": 1070,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-1 — simultaneous squarefree values: DIRECT NEW STAGE38 LEMMA",
      "startIndex": 1072,
      "endIndex": 1137,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Source:",
      "startIndex": 1138,
      "endIndex": 1145,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "preprints/Squarefree-values-of-quartics-and-power-free-values-of-polynomials-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex",
      "startIndex": 1146,
      "endIndex": 1275,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "and build/sections/02-sieve.tex.",
      "startIndex": 1276,
      "endIndex": 1308,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The openai/math corollary \"Separable products and simultaneous values\" says, for k=2, that a fixed finite family of separable integer polynomials whose irreducible factors have degree at most 4 has positive-density simultaneous squarefree values once the joint local condition #Omega_p < p^2 is verified for every prime p. Fixed finite congruence restrictions are compatible with the sieve transfer.",
      "startIndex": 1310,
      "endIndex": 1709,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Apply this to the Stage38 progression",
      "startIndex": 1711,
      "endIndex": 1748,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "u = 17627 + 34440 j",
      "startIndex": 1749,
      "endIndex": 1768,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "and the five integer polynomials",
      "startIndex": 1769,
      "endIndex": 1801,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "D(j) = u = 34440 j + 17627,",
      "startIndex": 1802,
      "endIndex": 1829,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "F(j) = 2u+729 = 68880 j + 35983,",
      "startIndex": 1830,
      "endIndex": 1862,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "E(j) = 4u+729 = 137760 j + 71237,",
      "startIndex": 1863,
      "endIndex": 1896,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "P7(j) = (8u^2-729^2)/7",
      "startIndex": 1897,
      "endIndex": 1919,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "      = 1355558400 j^2 + 1387597440 j + 355022513,",
      "startIndex": 1920,
      "endIndex": 1970,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "T41(j) = (8u^2+8*729*u+729^2)/41",
      "startIndex": 1971,
      "endIndex": 2003,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "       = 231436800 j^2 + 241805760 j + 63146857.",
      "startIndex": 2004,
      "endIndex": 2052,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "All five are primitive and separable; P7 and T41 are irreducible quadratics over Q. The prime support of every leading coefficient, both quadratic discriminants, and every pairwise resultant is contained in {2,3,5,7,41}. Thus for p outside {2,3,5,7,41}, all roots modulo p are simple and roots of different polynomials are disjoint. Hensel lifting gives at most",
      "startIndex": 2054,
      "endIndex": 2415,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1+1+1+2+2 = 7",
      "startIndex": 2416,
      "endIndex": 2429,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "bad residue classes modulo p^2, hence #Omega_p <= 7 < p^2.",
      "startIndex": 2430,
      "endIndex": 2488,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The five exceptional primes were checked exactly modulo p^2:",
      "startIndex": 2490,
      "endIndex": 2550,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "p=2: #Omega_2=0 of 4.",
      "startIndex": 2551,
      "endIndex": 2572,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "p=3: #Omega_3=0 of 9.",
      "startIndex": 2573,
      "endIndex": 2594,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "p=5: #Omega_5=0 of 25.",
      "startIndex": 2595,
      "endIndex": 2617,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "p=7: #Omega_7=1 of 49; only P7 contributes.",
      "startIndex": 2618,
      "endIndex": 2661,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "p=41: #Omega_41=1 of 1681; only T41 contributes.",
      "startIndex": 2662,
      "endIndex": 2710,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Therefore the joint local condition holds for every prime. The cited theorem gives a constant c>0 such that",
      "startIndex": 2712,
      "endIndex": 2819,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "#{1 <= j <= N : D(j),F(j),E(j),P7(j),T41(j) are all squarefree}",
      "startIndex": 2820,
      "endIndex": 2883,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "= c N + o(N).",
      "startIndex": 2884,
      "endIndex": 2897,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Conclusion: Stage38 now has an unconditional positive-density infinite clean-support subfamily on the forced progression. This is stronger than finite scans and W-8 heuristics. It does NOT imply that D,F,E are prime, that P7,T41 are semiprime, that R-8 factor shape occurs infinitely often, or that dim Sel2=2 has positive density.",
      "startIndex": 2899,
      "endIndex": 3230,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-2 — pointwise 2-converse: DIRECT BUT MOSTLY STRENGTHENING",
      "startIndex": 3232,
      "endIndex": 3294,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Sources:",
      "startIndex": 3295,
      "endIndex": 3303,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "preprints/A-pointwise-2-converse-for-elliptic-curves-with-rational-two-torsion-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex",
      "startIndex": 3304,
      "endIndex": 3432,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "preprints/Goldfelds-analytic-density-conjecture-and-the-2-converse-for-elliptic-curves-September-23-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex",
      "startIndex": 3433,
      "endIndex": 3572,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The finite criterion there is",
      "startIndex": 3574,
      "endIndex": 3603,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "d2(E)=dim_F2 Sel2(E/Q)-dim_F2 E(Q)[2].",
      "startIndex": 3604,
      "endIndex": 3642,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "If d2(E) is 0 or 1, then analytic rank = MW rank = full 2-infinity Selmer corank = d2, Sha is finite, and Sha[2-infinity]=0.",
      "startIndex": 3643,
      "endIndex": 3767,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "For Stage38 curves with full rational 2-torsion:",
      "startIndex": 3769,
      "endIndex": 3817,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- dim Sel2=2 gives d2=0, hence rank0 and vanishing Sha[2-infinity]. This strengthens the fixed-fiber conclusion but does not remove the separate torsion-point classification needed when one wants E(Q)=E[2].",
      "startIndex": 3818,
      "endIndex": 4024,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- B=+1 has dim Sel2=4, hence d2=2. The finite criterion does not apply.",
      "startIndex": 4025,
      "endIndex": 4096,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- CT-nondegenerate dim4 fibers already give MW rank0 by the Stage38 second-descent argument; the 2-converse can add analytic/Sha conclusions only after the full 2-power Selmer corank is shown small enough. It does not resolve the CT-zero fibers.",
      "startIndex": 4097,
      "endIndex": 4342,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification: USEFUL THEOREM STRENGTHENING, NOT THE MAIN FRONTIER SOLUTION.",
      "startIndex": 4344,
      "endIndex": 4421,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-3 — arithmetic graph realization / Address lemma: MAJOR METHOD, ADAPTER BLOCKED",
      "startIndex": 4423,
      "endIndex": 4507,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Source:",
      "startIndex": 4508,
      "endIndex": 4515,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "preprints/A-pointwise-2-converse-for-elliptic-curves-with-rational-two-torsion-September-24-2026/build/sections/graphs.tex.",
      "startIndex": 4516,
      "endIndex": 4639,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "This is the closest structural match to R-11/R-13. The source builds arithmetic graphs whose vertices are fresh primes, records local types and quadratic-residue bits, and proves:",
      "startIndex": 4641,
      "endIndex": 4820,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- finite simultaneous realization of prescribed forward residue bits at fresh primes while keeping all old vertices/data fixed;",
      "startIndex": 4821,
      "endIndex": 4948,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- product-label replacement by fresh primes;",
      "startIndex": 4949,
      "endIndex": 4993,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- an Address lemma that adds finitely many primary auxiliary prime vertices to force one or two binary graph symbols simultaneously at every nonzero Boolean address.",
      "startIndex": 4994,
      "endIndex": 5159,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "This is much stronger than ad hoc CRT forcing when its hypotheses hold.",
      "startIndex": 5161,
      "endIndex": 5232,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Direct Stage38 transfer is currently blocked. In Stage38 the graph vertices are prime divisors of the five coupled values D(u),F(u),E(u),P7(u),T41(u). They are not free prime factors that can simply be adjoined while holding the old parameter data fixed. A change of u changes the entire factorization and can introduce uncontrolled extra vertices. Therefore the Address lemma cannot presently be invoked to prove infinitely many dimSel2=2 or CT-nondegenerate fibers.",
      "startIndex": 5234,
      "endIndex": 5701,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Potential high-value adapter question:",
      "startIndex": 5703,
      "endIndex": 5741,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Can the Campedelli reduction be enlarged or reparametrized so that a finite set of designated support primes becomes freely insertable, while all uncontrolled cofactor primes enter only through a bounded stationary environment or a symbol that is provably insensitive to them?",
      "startIndex": 5742,
      "endIndex": 6018,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "If yes, this source could become a major uniformity engine. At present no such adapter is materialized.",
      "startIndex": 6019,
      "endIndex": 6122,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-4 — Monsky/Redei matrix constructions: METHOD CONFIRMATION",
      "startIndex": 6124,
      "endIndex": 6187,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Source:",
      "startIndex": 6188,
      "endIndex": 6195,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "preprints/Hilberts-tenth-problem-over-the-rational-numbers-September-24-2026/build/sections/03-parity.tex.",
      "startIndex": 6196,
      "endIndex": 6302,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The source gives explicit full-two-descent matrices for a full rational 2-torsion family, uses quadratic reciprocity identities of Monsky/Redei type, and constructs simultaneous kernel conditions by controlling Legendre-symbol data. This independently supports the architecture used in Stage38 R-11 through R-14: exact F2 matrix reduction is the right language.",
      "startIndex": 6304,
      "endIndex": 6665,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "But the curve family and freely chosen twist support differ from the K=729 one-parameter family. No literal matrix identity from this paper replaces the Stage38 tripartite matrix or proves its desired nullity uniformly.",
      "startIndex": 6667,
      "endIndex": 6886,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification: VALIDATION / DESIGN PATTERN, NO DIRECT CREDIT.",
      "startIndex": 6888,
      "endIndex": 6950,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-5 — Goldfeld / twist-density theorems: NO DIRECT ADAPTER",
      "startIndex": 6952,
      "endIndex": 7013,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Source:",
      "startIndex": 7014,
      "endIndex": 7021,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "preprints/Goldfelds-analytic-density-conjecture-and-the-2-converse-for-elliptic-curves-September-23-2026.",
      "startIndex": 7022,
      "endIndex": 7127,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The source proves rank-zero and rank-one density statements in a fixed quadratic-twist family. Stage38's E_u changes its Legendre ratio and j-invariant with u; it is not presently identified with the quadratic twists of one fixed elliptic curve. Therefore the 50/50 twist-density theorem cannot be transplanted to the u-family.",
      "startIndex": 7129,
      "endIndex": 7456,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification: NO DIRECT ADAPTER unless an exact isotrivial/fixed-twist reduction of a Stage38 subfamily is found.",
      "startIndex": 7458,
      "endIndex": 7573,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-6 — Cassels-Tate / 4-Selmer frontier",
      "startIndex": 7575,
      "endIndex": 7616,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A bounded search of openai/math for an explicit full-rational-2-torsion Sel4/second-2-descent formula that would directly decide Stage38's CT-zero dim4 fibers did not surface a ready theorem or implementation. The repository contains deep 2-primary Selmer-corank and Cassels-Tate infrastructure, but not a drop-in replacement for the current Stage38 tangent-form/Hilbert-symbol computation.",
      "startIndex": 7617,
      "endIndex": 8007,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The current Stage38 CT implementation therefore remains the sharper task-specific object. The main mathematical target is still to derive a uniform criterion or closed expression for the CT bit, or to compute enough 4-Selmer information to separate rank0 with larger Sha[4] from rank2.",
      "startIndex": 8009,
      "endIndex": 8294,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a bounded-search conclusion only, not a repository-wide absence claim.",
      "startIndex": 8296,
      "endIndex": 8374,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-7 — direct Campedelli/torsor closure search",
      "startIndex": 8376,
      "endIndex": 8424,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A bounded search for a direct Campedelli-surface rational-point theorem, Brauer-Manin closure theorem, or elementary-abelian-2 torsor result that would close R29-CAMP2 did not surface a ready adapter in openai/math. General abelian-cover/torsor material exists, but it does not supply the missing arithmetic obstruction for these specific quotients.",
      "startIndex": 8425,
      "endIndex": 8774,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification: NO DIRECT CLOSURE FOUND in the bounded review.",
      "startIndex": 8776,
      "endIndex": 8838,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Priority after the review",
      "startIndex": 8840,
      "endIndex": 8865,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1. Highest immediate value: promote/audit OM38-1 as a Stage38 lemma. It gives an unconditional positive-density infinite squarefree-support subfamily on the exact progression and is small enough for independent replay.",
      "startIndex": 8866,
      "endIndex": 9084,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Main frontier remains CT/4-Selmer for dimSel2=4. The openai/math review did not eliminate this bottleneck.",
      "startIndex": 9085,
      "endIndex": 9194,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "3. High-upside structural research: test whether the R-11 tripartite graph can be embedded in the openai arithmetic-graph realization framework despite the polynomial-value coupling. This requires an exact cofactor-insensitivity or bounded-environment lemma; without it, do not claim Address-lemma applicability.",
      "startIndex": 9195,
      "endIndex": 9507,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "4. Do not spend time trying to force R-8's prime/semiprime factor shape from the squarefree theorem; squarefree positive density is strictly weaker.",
      "startIndex": 9508,
      "endIndex": 9656,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "5. Existing authority/credit/closure flags remain unchanged.",
      "startIndex": 9657,
      "endIndex": 9717,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "OM38-1 exact local-admissibility audit data",
      "startIndex": 9719,
      "endIndex": 9762,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_1",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Quadratic discriminants:",
      "startIndex": 9763,
      "endIndex": 9787,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "disc(P7)=2^11 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 41^2.",
      "startIndex": 9788,
      "endIndex": 9822,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "disc(T41)=2^11 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 7^2.",
      "startIndex": 9823,
      "endIndex": 9857,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Prime supports of the ten pairwise resultants:",
      "startIndex": 9859,
      "endIndex": 9905,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(D,F): 2^3 * 3^7 * 5 * 7 * 41.",
      "startIndex": 9906,
      "endIndex": 9939,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(D,E): 2^3 * 3^7 * 5 * 7 * 41.",
      "startIndex": 9940,
      "endIndex": 9973,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(D,P7): 2^6 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 7 * 41^2.",
      "startIndex": 9974,
      "endIndex": 10013,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(D,T41): 2^6 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 7^2 * 41.",
      "startIndex": 10014,
      "endIndex": 10054,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(F,E): 2^4 * 3^7 * 5 * 7 * 41.",
      "startIndex": 10055,
      "endIndex": 10088,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(F,P7): 2^8 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 7 * 41^2.",
      "startIndex": 10089,
      "endIndex": 10128,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(F,T41): 2^8 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 7^2 * 41.",
      "startIndex": 10129,
      "endIndex": 10169,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(E,P7): 2^9 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 7 * 41^2.",
      "startIndex": 10170,
      "endIndex": 10209,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(E,T41): 2^9 * 3^14 * 5^2 * 7^2 * 41.",
      "startIndex": 10210,
      "endIndex": 10250,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Res(P7,T41): 2^20 * 3^28 * 5^4 * 7^2 * 41^2.",
      "startIndex": 10251,
      "endIndex": 10295,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Thus outside {2,3,5,7,41}, the five reductions have disjoint simple roots and the total number of roots modulo p^2 is at most seven.",
      "startIndex": 10297,
      "endIndex": 10429,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Exact exceptional-prime enumeration:",
      "startIndex": 10431,
      "endIndex": 10467,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- p=2,3,5: no residue j modulo p^2 makes any of the five values divisible by p^2.",
      "startIndex": 10468,
      "endIndex": 10549,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- p=7: the joint bad set is exactly j=3 modulo49, coming from P7 only.",
      "startIndex": 10550,
      "endIndex": 10620,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "- p=41: the joint bad set is exactly j=895 modulo1681, coming from T41 only.",
      "startIndex": 10621,
      "endIndex": 10697,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    },
    {
      "text": "This supplies a deterministic finite audit of the only exceptional local factors.",
      "startIndex": 10699,
      "endIndex": 10780,
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false
    }
  ]
